Claude CodeClaude Desktop / CursorGemini CLICodexHTTP <pre><code>pip install "pardesline[mcp]"
claude mcp add pardesline -- pardesline mcp
</code></pre> <p>The repository also ships <code>.mcp.json</code> (picked up when you open the repo) and a Claude Code plugin manifest (<code>.claude-plugin/plugin.json</code>) that declares the server and the twenty skills.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pardesline": { "command": "pardesline", "args": ["mcp"] }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Claude Desktop: <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>. Cursor: Settings → MCP → add server, or <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> in the project.</p> <p>Add the same block to <code>~/.gemini/settings.json</code>.</p> <pre><code>[mcp_servers.pardesline]
command = "pardesline"
args = ["mcp"]
</code></pre> <pre><code>pardesline mcp --transport streamable-http --port 8765     # http://127.0.0.1:8765/mcp
</code></pre> <p>When <code>pardesline</code> is not on <code>PATH</code>, use <code>python -m pardesline.mcp_server</code> as the command.</p>
